From f7865eee90797d61ffb6f00144f573add2c68972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 04:49:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH v2 21/21] FEXInterpreter: hold log messages until the log
 destination is known

FEXInterpreter installs its message handler before the config is loaded,
and until Logging::Init() reads SilentLog and OutputLog that handler
writes to stderr. Everything logged while connecting to or starting
FEXServer (connection errors, "FEXServer returned empty rootfs path;
keeping configured value") therefore went to the guest's stderr whatever
the log settings were, and broke programs that capture or compare it.

Messages logged before Init() are now held in a fixed 8 KB buffer (the
allocator isn't set up yet) and replayed to the configured destination
once it is known: the server log, a file, stderr when OutputLog=stderr
is asked for, or nowhere when logging is silent (the default). Asserts
still print immediately, since the process is about to trap. If the
client can't be set up at all, the guest never runs and the held
messages are flushed to stderr as the only explanation.

With OutputLog=server and no log FD from the server, logging now goes
silent instead of falling back to stderr.

Evidence, 64K host, FEX_HOSTPAGEMODE=force, static x86-64 hello with the
server start race from the previous patch provoked: stderr went from
1639 bytes to 1139, the host page size warning alone (printed directly,
on purpose).

v2, replacing held patch 0015. Review: "hides FEXServer and rootfs errors
under our default-silent logging." With silent logging, Init() now keeps
the held ERROR and ASSERT messages (debug and info ones are still dropped)
and FlushHeldErrorsToStderr writes them to stderr when the process fails:
any start-up failure return in main, a nonzero guest status at the end of
main, or exit_group with a nonzero status (new
FEX::HLE::GuestErrorExitHook). A forked child does not repeat its parent's.
A successful run still prints nothing. The server exec failure messages,
logged in a child that exits at once, go straight to stderr.
"FEXServer returned empty rootfs path" is logged only when the configured
rootfs is a squashfs/EroFS image: with no rootfs or a directory an empty
answer is normal, and at error level it would print after every guest that
exits nonzero.

64K host, FEX_HOSTPAGEMODE=force, a Config.json whose RootFS value is an
object, static x86-64 test:
  guest exits 1:  v1 nothing; v2 "E JSON file '.../Config.json': Couldn't
                  get value for config item 'RootFS'"
  guest succeeds: both print only the guest's output
  no config error, guest exits 1: both print nothing
